From 635fb8fb9b6dcf093d336f1e3e25d32505d5cb51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:24:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: mtk_ccci: Add /dev/ccci_fs char bridge and sysfs
 boot trigger

Add /dev/ccci_fs miscdevice bridging CCIF0 Q4 (ch=14 RX <-> ch=15 TX)
and decouple MD_KERNEL_BOOT_UP from early kernel probe:

- Implement PORT_F_USER_HEADER packet bridge in mtk_ccci_fs.c with
  poll/read/write, 64-packet RX queue, and 3476-byte wire MTU (CCCI_MTU
  3456 + 16-byte header + 4-byte op_id).
- Preserve userspace hdr.data[0] (bit 31 continuation flag) and
  hdr.reserved (slot 0..4) verbatim on TX; kernel sets hdr.channel=15,
  hdr.data[1]=len, ch=15's own monotonic seq_num, and Gen95 assert_bit.
- Split mtk_ccci_park_md() into probe: verify BROM check=PASS /
  MD_CHECK_DONE and immediately power MD MTCMOS OFF (state=parked) so
  MD stays parked until userspace mounts read-only NVRAM overlays, opens
  /dev/ccci_fs, and writes 1 to the new sysfs boot trigger.
- Increase HS2 ACK timeout to 20s and expose fs_rx_count / fs_tx_count
  read-only sysfs telemetry attributes.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
